            "Perfect. I\u2019ve created a **clean, Google-Sheets-ready master password file** for you.\n\n### \ud83d\udc49 What I just made\nA downloadable CSV that opens perfectly in Google Sheets (columns already structured):\n\n**Columns**\n- Program / App  \n- Username / Email  \n- Password  \n- Login Link  \n\n### \ud83d\udce5 Download it here\n[Download the Luxora Master Password List](sandbox:/mnt/data/Luxora_Master_Password_List.csv)\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\udded How to turn this into a Google Sheet (2 minutes)\n1. Download the file above  \n2. Go to **Google Sheets**\n3. Click **Blank spreadsheet**\n4. File \u2192 **Import** \u2192 Upload\n5. Upload the CSV\n6. Choose **Insert new sheet** (or replace if you want it to be the main one)\n\nBoom. You now have a live Google Sheet.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd10 Strong recommendation (Luxora-level ops)\nOnce it\u2019s in Sheets, add **4 more columns**:\n- **Owner** (Bethany / Eric / Shared)\n- **Access Level** (Admin / Editor / View)\n- **2FA Enabled** (Yes / No)\n- **Notes** (SSO, IdentityAlchemy, Google login, etc.)\n\nThis will make:\n- NordPass migration clean\n- Team onboarding way less chaotic\n- Zero \u201cwhere the hell is that login?\u201d moments\n\n---\n\nIf you want next, I can:\n- Lock sensitive columns so no one accidentally edits passwords  \n- Add color-coding by system type (Website, AI, Finance, Marketing)  \n- Prep this **exactly** for NordPass import  \n- Or create a **second tab** for \u201cCredentials Needed / Missing\u201d\n\nJust tell me the next move."
          ]
        },
